# MDD - processing

## Installation

To install package run:
```
pip install git+ssh://git@github.com/Postup-Solutions/mdd-processing.git
```

If you need files for magnetometer calibration (Systeminfo files), you can run:
```
 mkdir sys_in
 cd sys_in/
 git init
 git remote add -f origin git@github.com:Postup-Solutions/mdd-processing.git
 git config core.sparseCheckout true
 echo "system_info" > .git/info/sparse-checkout
 git pull origin main
 mv  system_info/* .
 rm -r system_info/
 rm -r .git
```

Example of usage:
```
from mdd_processing import run_preprocessing as rp

# pass True if you want to log to the log file and terminal
# and False if you want to log just to terminal
rp.setup_logger(False)

fpc = rp.FileProcessConfig(
    mdd_filepath=".../20250325_121959_MD-R3_#0055.mdd",
    systeminfo_filepath="sys_in/SystemInfo_#0055.txt",
    delimiter=";",
    result_filepath="res.asc"
)

rp.process_single_file(fpc)
```
If you are using `mdd_filepath`, than code is going to produce an additional `mdd_filepath_RF.csv` file, that represents decoded mdd file.  
This file can be passed to the `process_single_file` function with `src_filepath` parameter.

## Obfuscation

Build with Nuitka for a complied, obfuscated package

```
pip install -e ".[dev]"
python scripts/build_nuitka.py
```

Output in 'dist/' 


